=== Climate ===
Gunma Prefecture has a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification ''Cfa''), characterized by hot, humid summers and mild winters. The Katsuran-facing coast, sheltered from the full force of the Shendan monsoon, receives significantly less rainfall than the eastern Ishijima coast—approximately 1,920 mm annually compared to Ishijima Prefecture's 3,200 mm. The Asuka Range creates a pronounced rain shadow effect, with the western slopes receiving moderate precipitation while the eastern Ishijima coast bears the brunt of the monsoon.

The interior highlands experience cooler temperatures and more pronounced seasonal variation than the coastal plain. The mountain communities near the Asuka massif regularly see winter temperatures drop below freezing, and the highest elevations support persistent snow cover from June through September.

